```text
changes, and that he will share a copy of the proposed changes with the private haulers following
City attorney review and approval.  Motion to postpone carried.  Voting “yes” -- all members of
the governing body present.
“An Ordinance amending various sections of Chapter 5.36, Circuses, Carnivals,
Exhibitions, and Amusement Rides, within Title 5, Business Licenses and Regulations, of the
Cheyenne City Code.”  Mr. Valdez moved to approve on second reading, seconded by Mr.
Spiker.  Discussion followed regarding wording of certain sections of the ordinance with Bruce
Wilson, Chief Building Official, explaining that a request to amend by substitute would be made
at the next Finance Committee to correct editorial errors.  Discussion continued on reason for
removal of current City Code wording involving garbage, refuse and water fees; illumination
requirements involving a change from 5 foot candles to 1 foot candles; assembly of rides; current
and proposed ride inspection process, and Level Three National Association of Amusement Ride
Safety Official (NAARSO) requirement and responsible party to provide/hire a NAARSO
certified inspector to conduct ride inspections.  During discussion, Mr. Wilson provided
information on topics raised.  Concerns were expressed regarding insurance criteria and proof of
coverage, party/parties responsible for retaining services of the NAARSO inspector; inspection
procedures during ride set-up and final inspection; ride safety issues, and current potential City
liability connected with Building inspectors providing initial ride inspections.  Upon inquiry,
Dan White, City Attorney, advised an owner or licensee of an amusement ride, or the insurance
company providing coverage, can retain the NAARSO certified inspector, noting the inspection
has to be accepted by the insurance company before it will issue the coverage policy so the
safeguard for the City is the requirement that a copy of the ride inspection certificate and
insurance policy must be in place before the ride is put into operation.  Upon inquiry, Mr.
Wilson reviewed concerns with Building inspectors providing ride inspections once a year vs. a
NAARSCO certified inspector who is the most familiar with the elements of ride inspections.
Mr. White reviewed risks associated with having City employees inspecting the rides and stated
the ordinance will reduce the City’s liability risk.  John Volk, insurance agent, provided
information on insurance coverages generally.  Mike White, Building Department inspector,
provided information on the NAARSO certified inspector who is involved with inspection of
rides for the Cheyenne Frontier Days celebration, stating the inspector is hired by the owner’s
insurance company and is very highly regarded and qualified in the industry.  Motion carried.
Voting “yes” -- all members of the governing body present.
“An Ordinance submitting to the qualified property owners of real property within the
