Consideration of Bid #R-21-11 for furnishing 76 new computers and operating systems
for the City of Cheyenne, Information Technology Division (2007-2010 1% Sales Tax Capital
Equipment fund).  Mr. Valdez moved to accept the bid from Howard Industries, Inc., Laurel,
MS, in an amount not to exceed $39,672.00, seconded by Mr. Brown.  Upon inquiry, Tyler
Nelson, Assistant Director, Information Technology Division, provided information on the age
of the computers that will be replaced; software compatibility issues involving older computers
and the Division’s annual user replacement plan.  Concern was expressed with the City’s Lotus
Notes e-mail system and effects of not acquiring the proposed equipment for a year to possibly
utilize the funds to acquire a different e-mail system.  Mr. Nelson confirmed the e-mail software
being used is up-to-date and is comparable to other software, and stated upgrading to a new e-
mail system would be more costly than the funding that is available for the proposed annual
equipment purchases. Theresa Snyder, Director of Information Technology, reviewed Lotus
Notes’ functionality elements; implementation of the software program pursuant to past City
Council direction, history of the annual equipment replacement plan and effects on users if the
plan were not in place, and explained the process entailed in researching e-mail documents
pursuant to a recent request for public records.  Comments followed on use of 5 penny money,
th
as authorized by voters through the 1% ballot question, for the purchase vs. an e-mail system,
and cost per computer per the bid submitted.  Ms. Snyder advised the bid amount was the lowest
that has been received in past years, and Mr. Nelson explained the cost of a business class work
station computer is different, including maintenance/replacement provisions, than the cost of a
computer for home use.  Motion carried.  Voting “yes” -- all members of the governing body
present.
[CA]
