Electric, Cheyenne, Wyoming, for the Brimmer Park Lighting Correction project (Partial 2007-
2010 1% Sales Tax and Energy Grant funds).  Motion (per Consent Agenda) carried (amount not
to exceed $59,500.00). (#5650)
Consideration of Bid #M-7-11 for a contract between the City of Cheyenne and Scotch
Boy,  Inc., Cheyenne, Wyoming, for the David R. Romero South Cheyenne Youth Activity and
Community Center project (Partial Community Facility fees and donations).  Mr. Valdez moved
to accept the bid in an amount not to exceed $156,614.18, seconded by Mr. Pierson.  Mr. Valdez
moved to amend by substitute which reduces the not to exceed amount to $137,206.48, seconded
by Mr. Pierson.  Motion to amend carried.  Voting “yes” -- all members of the governing body
present.  Main motion as amended carried.  Voting “yes” -- all members of the governing body
present. (#5651)
Consideration of Bid #R-22-11 for furnishing one new rough mower from Greenline
Equipment, Casper, Wyoming, for the Grounds and Facilities Division (2007-2010 1% Sales
Tax Capital Equipment fund).  Jason Sanchez, Director of Grounds and Facilities, explained the
need for the new mower that has a wider swath and is more fuel efficient, stating 2 mowers
would be involved as trade-ins.  He discussed maintenance costs and downtime being incurred
with the current mower model; companies who submitted bids and the different models that
```

### Page 10 of 13

```text
were bid; purpose for issuance of an addendum to the bid that allowed acceptance of another
bidder, and maintenance, equipment replacement and service requirements outlined in the bid
document.  Aaron Morrison, Greenline Equipment, provided an update on revisions and
improvements that have been made to the type of mower unit submitted in the bid and stated past
models have experienced problems in such areas as air circulation, hydraulics, valves and the
motordeck. He confirmed Greenline can meet the 24 hour response service and equipment
replacement requirements.  Mr. Valdez moved to approve the bid submitted by Greenline
Equipment, Casper, WY, in an amount not to exceed $27,826.00, seconded by Mr. Pierson.
Upon inquiry regarding any needed equipment repairs, Mr. Morrison clarified the machine could
be returned to Casper for repair, or a basic repair might be done on-site through a company
mobile repair unit, and they would do whatever needed to be done within the 24 hour repair
time. Upon inquiry, Mr. Sanchez explained it was difficult for him to make a recommendation
on the low bid submitted based on past maintenance cost and downtime experience involving the
current mower.  He noted that Greenline met bid specifications, have submitted documentation
supporting improvements to the mower unit contained in their bid, and that Greenline was the
lowest bidder.  Upon inquiry, Mr. Morrison provided equipment warranty information for the
model that was bid.  Discussion included: Bid specifications generally vs. by specific
models/brands; purchasing procedures; maintenance cost and equipment reliability concerns;
warranty, and bid tabulation/recommendation information issued by the Purchasing Division.
Motion carried.  Voting “yes” -- all members of the governing body present with the exception
of Mr. Spiker voting “no”.
