Announcement was made of the appointment of Dr. Mark Rinne to the Downtown
Development Authority Board to be confirmed March 28, 2011.
Under other business:
Ms. Broyles inquired about the status of a liquor licensee who had failed Police
Department underage compliance checks pursuant to review of annual liquor licensee renewals.
Carol Intlekofer, City Clerk, advised representatives from the establishment were present at the
Finance Committee meeting, but no questions were posed to them.  Comments included
indication that the licensee involved has indicated TIPS training would be provided to employees
and time frame, per City Code, in which employees must receive training.  Ms. Intlekofer noted
that Police Chief Brian Kozak and Officer Steve Neisen had discussed City Code wording
regarding the time frame for training at the last City Council meeting and had indicated a review
should be made to see if any clarification changes should be considered.
There being no further business to come before the governing body, Mayor Kaysen
adjourned the meeting at 9:34 p.m.
Submitted by,
Carol Intlekofer, MMC
City Clerk
